## Context
Ticket 0085 routes `erg COMMAND --help` to the global printUsage() list —
a minimal fix. This ticket goes further: serve the full doc comment for the
specific command, so `erg close --help` prints the three-step close semantics,
not just `close ID REASON [DIR]   Close a ticket atomically`.

The doc comments written in 0089 are the source. This ticket wires them to
the --help dispatch.

## Actions
1. Add a `helpText map[string]string` in main.go, keyed by command name,
   containing each cmdXxx doc comment as a string constant (or extracted
   via go:embed from a generated file).
2. In the --help guard loop (added by 0084), if the command is known, print
   the per-command help and exit 0; if unknown, fall back to printUsage().
3. Global `erg --help` (no subcommand) keeps printing printUsage() summary.

## Test
`erg close --help` must include "Inserts a Closed: REASON header".
`erg --help` must still print the short command list.
Output must go to stdout.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg COMMAND --help` prints the full doc comment for that command
- [ ] Unknown command `--help` falls back to global usage
- [ ] `erg --help` prints the short list (unchanged)
- [ ] `make test` passes
